From acd167500e7ae628aa7b17799be046c2bb67b40a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 17:07:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 50/70] fix(polecat): re-provision nuked polecats instead of
 stranding them as free capacity (hq-c899)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

hq-fqap made nuked polecats (identity kept, worktree removed) count as
reusable/free capacity. But the allocator could not actually use them:
FindIdlePolecat now returns them, ReuseIdlePolecat then fails closed on
its worktree stat, and reclaimBrokenIdlePolecatForSling refuses to reclaim
them (agent_state=nuked guard protects the CV chain) -> the slot fell
through to a fresh spawn under a NEW name, losing the identity, and every
sling cycle logged "not safe to reclaim: agent_state=nuked".

Add Manager.ReuseOrRepairIdlePolecat: a lock-free dispatcher that stats
the worktree and routes to fast branch-only reuse when it exists, or to
RepairWorktreeWithOptions (re-provision in place, force=true) when it is
structurally missing. A nuked polecat is thus reactivated under its own
identity/CV chain instead of stranded. The check is lock-free so it does
not nest the per-polecat lock the delegates take.

SpawnPolecatForSling now calls ReuseOrRepairIdlePolecat, and
reclaimBrokenIdlePolecatForSling skips reusable (nuked) polecats — leaving
them for the repair path — so only genuinely non-reusable broken polecats
are removed for a fresh spawn. This also silences the per-cycle reclaim
warning storm.

Tests: ReuseOrRepairIdlePolecat re-provisions a missing worktree preserving
identity + working state; healthy worktree takes branch-only reuse without
moving the clone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
